      ""rationale"": ""The patient presents with classic signs of lateral medullary infarction: Horner syndrome (ipsilateral), ataxia (ipsilateral limb incoordination), crossed sensory loss (ipsilateral facial pain/temperature loss and contralateral body pain/temperature loss), dysphagia and absent gag reflex (ipsilateral), and dysarthria. These findings localize to the left lateral medulla. The left vertebral artery occlusion on CTA supports this diagnosis.""
