      ""question"": ""What is the most likely diagnosis based on the history and examination findings?"",
      ""my_answer"": ""Motion sickness."",
      ""rationale"": ""The patient has recurrent nausea and dizziness exclusively during car travel, particularly on winding roads, with symptoms resolving quickly after stopping. Improvement with sitting in the front seat and looking out the window is characteristic. No other neurological or otologic symptoms or signs are present, and the exam is normal, making motion sickness the most consistent diagnosis.""
