elf-care appropriate;Pediatrics;0.0;8.0;"{
  ""sub_questions"": [
    {
      ""id"": ""Q1"",
      ""question"": ""What is the most likely diagnosis based on the clinical presentation and epidemiology?"",
      ""my_answer"": ""Hand, foot, and mouth disease (HFMD) caused by enterovirus, likely Coxsackievirus A16."",
      ""rationale"": ""The combination of low-grade fever, oral ulcers, and vesicular lesions on the hands and feet in a 3-year-old, especially with a history of similar cases in daycare, is classic for HFMD. The age group, seasonal context (common in daycare settings), and characteristic distribution of lesions support this diagnosis.""
    },
