      ""id"": ""Q5"",
      ""question"": ""What fetal monitoring abnormalities indicate fetal hypoxia and impending demise?"",
      ""my_answer"": ""Baseline tachycardia (170 bpm), absent variability, and repetitive late decelerations constitute a category III tracing indicating fetal metabolic acidemia and poor reserve."",
