      ""rationale"": ""Topical antibiotics prevent secondary infection. Avoiding contact lenses reduces infection and healing complications. Cycloplegics help alleviate pain due to ciliary spasm and photophobia. Patching is not routinely recommended due to risk of complications and limited benefit. Follow-up ensures healing and absence of complications like corneal ulceration.""
