      ""rationale"": ""Streptococcal pharyngitis presents with fever and exudative pharyngitis but typically lacks systemic features like fatigue and petechiae. EBV mononucleosis matches well with age, pharyngitis, lymphadenopathy, and palatal petechiae. Acute HIV can mimic mononucleosis with fever, pharyngitis, rash, and lymphadenopathy, and must be ruled out in sexually active adolescents.""
    },
