      ""question"": ""Which specialty should lead the initial management of this patient?"",
      ""my_answer"": ""General Surgery."",
      ""rationale"": ""Surgical management, typically appendectomy, is the standard of care for acute appendicitis with signs of perforation. The presence of a contained fluid collection increases complexity and necessitates surgical input for definitive treatment.""
