    ""The patient's hyperthermia may not solely be due to prolonged muscle activity; infectious causes such as central nervous system infection should be considered as potential contributing or precipitating factors."",
    ""Irregular respiratory pattern raises concern for brainstem involvement or impending respiratory arrest, a sign of neurologic deterioration."",
    ""Although finger-stick glucose is normal, metabolic disturbances like hyponatremia or liver dysfunction (which can alter drug metabolism) may still contribute and must be ruled out."",
