      ""question"": ""Does this patient have acute adrenal crisis?"",
      ""my_answer"": ""Yes"",
      ""rationale"": ""The patient has known Addison disease, missed stress-dose glucocorticoid replacement due to vomiting, and presents with classic signs of adrenal crisis: hypotension unresponsive to fluids, hyponatremia, hyperkalemia, hypoglycemia, hyperpigmentation, and a critically low random cortisol. This constellation strongly confirms adrenal crisis.""
    },
    {
