      ""question"": ""What is the initial management for this patient?"",
      ""my_answer"": ""Topical antifungal agents (e.g., clotrimazole, terbinafine) twice daily for 2–4 weeks, along with hygiene measures (drying feet thoroughly, wearing flip-flops in showers, changing socks daily)."",
      ""rationale"": ""Topical azoles or allylamines are first-line for limited tinea pedis. Given the non-inflammatory, interdigital form, systemic therapy is not needed. Hygiene modification reduces reinfection risk, especially in athletes using communal facilities.""
